Step 9 — Get YumePet on your teammate's computer
After they accept the invitation, your teammate should:
1. Install Git and Node.js if not already installed.
2. Open Git Bash in the folder where they want to keep the project.
3. Run:
git clone https://github.com/jastona0-arch/YumePet.git
cd YumePet
npm install
npm run dev


They will then have their own local copy of YumePet.
Step 10 — Keep both copies synchronized
Whenever you make new changes, upload them using:
git add .
git commit -m "Describe your changes"
git push


Before starting new work, your teammate should run:
git pull


For now, have your teammate accept the invitation and clone the repository.
